WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.200
NARRATOR: Spider-Man has always
been amazing and spectacular.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.570
But it took a mind swap with
one of his greatest enemies

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:07.600
to make him--

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.390
 Superior in every
way, superior strength,

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.060
superior intellect,
superior skills.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.220
NARRATOR: And a
superior ego, yeesh.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.020
Get ready to learn
the full story of how

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.600
Otto Octavius became
the Superior Spider-Man,

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.170
on Marvel's Long Story Short.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.470
DOCTOR OCTOPUS: Right
in the tentacles.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.180
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.160
NARRATOR: Doctor Octopus
was a super-scientist

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.620
who became a supervillain
after one of his experiments

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.520
went horribly wrong.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.379
 Um, mind narrowing that down?

00:00:32.379 --> 00:00:33.790
That could be a
lot of my villains.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.150
 Dolt, you know he's
talking about me.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.560
When my amazing mechanical
limbs fused to my spine,

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:39.985
I became the greatest
criminal mastermind

00:00:39.985 --> 00:00:42.120
in New York City And I-

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.937
 Why don't you let the
narrator do his job, Doc?

00:00:43.937 --> 00:00:44.770
NARRATOR: Thanks, Spidey.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:45.910
 I got you.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:48.520
NARRATOR: Spider-Man spent years
foiling the Doc's evil schemes

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.960
and fighting him, mostly
on subways and bridges.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.193
 It's where I do my best work.

00:00:52.193 --> 00:00:53.560
NARRATOR: But years
of fights took a toll

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.120
on the Doc's very human body.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.800
And he did what any mad
scientist approaching

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:57.950
death's door would do.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.900
 Accept the inevitable and
make amends with all those

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:00.700
he had wronged?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.740
NARRATOR: Nope, switch brains
with his greatest enemy.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.080
[SIZZLING AND YELLING]

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.260
Doctor Octopus was now in
Spider-Man's body with access

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.280
to all of his powers.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.663
 And I shall use
them to conquer.

00:01:10.663 --> 00:01:11.830
NARRATOR: But he
was also empowered

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.210
with Spider-Man's conscience.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.910
 You ain't getting rid
of me that easy, Doc.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.445
 Oh, pooh, being bad
doesn't feel fun anymore.

00:01:17.445 --> 00:01:18.550
NARRATOR: And so,
in that moment,

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.710
Doctor Octopus vowed
to become the hero he

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.400
could never be in his own life.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.230
He would become--

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:26.740
 The Superior Spider-Man, for
with great power, there must

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.900
also come great responsibility.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.730
 Now you're stealing
my lines too?

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:32.380
NARRATOR: For several
months, Otto Octavius

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.570
patrolled the streets
of NYC as Spider-Man.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.850
And for an only recently
reformed supervillain,

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:37.930
he did a lot of good.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.500
He stopped villains
like the Vulture--

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.300
 Too easy.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.540
NARRATOR: The Sinister Six--

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.817
 There's actually some
appeal to this hero thing.

00:01:43.817 --> 00:01:44.950
NARRATOR: --and
the Spider-Slayer.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.750
 Perhaps this is
my true calling.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.000
NARRATOR: He even gained some
unlikely fans in the process.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:49.960
 I don't know what it is.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.830
But there's something I like
about you now, Web-head.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:52.450
[HMPH]

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:53.650
 You all make it
sound like he was

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.030
a better Spider-Man than me.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.590
 And a better Peter Parker.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.540
I spend more time with
Aunt May and moved

00:01:58.540 --> 00:01:59.750
in with my new girlfriend.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:00.550
 What's up, Slick?

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.580
 And I went back to
school to get my doctorate.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.890
 You had time for that?

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.420
 It's called
multitasking, Peter.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:06.220
Look into it.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.453
NARRATOR: In a lot
of ways, he really

00:02:07.453 --> 00:02:08.664
was the Superior Spider-Man.

00:02:08.664 --> 00:02:09.900
 Come one, narrator.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.380
How about a little
back up, here?

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:13.690
NARRATOR: Well, he also did
some very non-Spider-Man things,

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.970
like open up a secret lair
off the coast of Manhattan

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.870
and cover the city in an
army of robot spiders.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:18.780
 I knew it.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.347
 Well, old evil
habits to die hard.

00:02:21.347 --> 00:02:22.480
NARRATOR: But with
the Spider-Bots

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.840
patrolling the entire city,
overall crime did go way down.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.550
Unfortunately, the
Green Goblin hacked

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.790
the Spider-Bots, allowing
Goblin-related crime

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:30.590
to go way up.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:31.390
[SIGH]

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.100
Eventually, Norman
Osborn was able to take

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:35.080
full control of the
Spider-Bots and used

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.340
them to take over the city.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.880
 And I stole your
girlfriend, Spider-Man.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.080
NARRATOR: Knowing
that only the real

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.790
Spider-Man could save the
day, Doctor Octopus realized--

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.530
 I must give Peter Parker
control of his body back,

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.900
for he is the
Superior Spider-Man.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:48.796
[SIZZLING AND YELLING]

00:02:48.796 --> 00:02:51.040
 I'm back.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.350
NARRATOR: And now
you know the truth

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.480
behind the Superior
Spider-Man, thanks

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.280
to Marvel's Long Story Short.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.010
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.160
 I still like the
other guy better.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.910
[MUSIC PLAYING]

